From 2b08169fe83d255127481000e4867a43a31c895b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:58:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 38/39] Runtime: input bindings from input.ini

The host pad mapping was hard-coded twice: PSPadBackend::readState
(ps2_pad.cpp, the one the runner uses: scePadRead always asks the backend
first) and an older, different fallback in Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp (reached only
without a runtime, i.e. in unit tests). Both now read one table,
runtime/ps2_input_bindings.h, built once at start-up.

- PS2Runtime::initialize loads PS2X_INPUT_INI=<path>, else <exe dir>/input.ini
  when present; no file = the defaults, which are exactly PSPadBackend's old
  mapping (gamepad 0 when present and then only it; else the keyboard: arrows
  and WASD as the d-pad, X/SPACE cross, C/ESCAPE circle, Z/KP_0 square,
  V/KP_1 triangle, Q/E L1/R1, LEFT_SHIFT/RIGHT_SHIFT L2/R2, ENTER start, TAB
  select; axes 128 + v * 127, no dead zone).
- Sections [keyboard] and [gamepad]; one entry per PS2 button (up down left
  right cross circle square triangle l1 r1 l2 r2 l3 r3 start select), several
  raylib names comma-separated (without KEY_ / GAMEPAD_BUTTON_, any case);
  stick_left/stick_right (keyboard: four keys up, down, left, right; gamepad:
  two axes x, y); gamepad device (0..3) and deadzone (0..1, per axis, the rest
  rescaled). Empty or NONE unbinds. A bad line is printed once as
  "[input] line N: ..." and its entry keeps its value.
- Per poll: the same raylib calls as before (one per bound code, stopping at
  the first held one per button).
- Tests: the defaults reproduce the old mapping key by key, button by button,
  axis by axis (22 key polls); a file overrides a binding and the others keep
  their defaults (also through PS2X_INPUT_INI); bad lines are reported once
  each and fall back; the dead zone centres and rescales the axes.
